* ADG5248F Analog Multiplexer Netlist
.lib ADG.lib

* Power Supplies (+/-15V)
V_VDD VDD 0 15
V_VSS VSS 0 -15

* Logic Power / Enable (5V)
V_EN EN 0 5

* Channel Select (Channel 1 -> A0=0, A1=0, A2=0)
V_A0 A0 0 0
V_A1 A1 0 0
V_A2 A2 0 0

* Input Signal: 1 kHz, 500 mV amplitude sine wave
V_IN IN 0 SINE(0 0.5 1k)

* Device Under Test: ADG5248F
* Typical ADI pin order for 8:1 fault-protected mux: 
* S1 S2 S3 S4 S5 S6 S7 S8 D A0 A1 A2 EN VDD VSS GND FF SF
X1 IN 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 OUT A0 A1 A2 EN VDD VSS 0 FF SF ADG5248F

* Output Load
R_LOAD OUT 0 1Meg

* Pull-ups for Fault Flags (typically open drain)
R_FF VDD FF 10k
R_SF VDD SF 10k

* Transient Analysis (5ms run to capture 5 cycles at 1kHz)
.tran 1u 5m

* Measure peak-to-peak voltages over the settled cycles to determine gain
.measure tran VOUT_PP PP V(OUT) FROM=2m TO=5m
.measure tran VIN_PP PP V(IN) FROM=2m TO=5m
.measure tran gain_db PARAM 20*log10(VOUT_PP/VIN_PP)

.end
